    "prompt": "Find the domain of $f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x-1}}{x-4}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$D=[1,4)\\cup(4,\\infty)$.\n\nCombine $x\\ge1$ from the square root with $x\\ne4$ from the denominator.",
      "worked": "The numerator requires $x\\ge1$ for the square root to be real. The denominator requires $x\\ne4$.\n\nBoth restrictions must hold, so the domain is\n$$D=[1,4)\\cup(4,\\infty).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
